          <br><br>
          <h3 style="text-align: center;">Engaging Congregations in Diakonia</h3>
          <br><br>
          CONGREGATION LEADERS and pastors often
          ask me, “What can a deaconess do for us?”
          In this specialized American culture, they
          are usually looking for a job description.
          However, the most accurate response I can give is: the dea-
          coness will walk among your congregation to its
          diaconal work.
          <br><br>
          Since opportunities for diakonia are limit-
          less, the deaconess is not in danger of work-
          ing herself out of a job. However, the dia-
          coness must be established. She really
          exists only until the congregations are joined
          in preaching and diakonia, as husband and wife
          are joined. So, she is a spiritual worker,
          the heartbeat of this marriage would look like
          a steady, sinuous rhythm of worship to works and
          back to worship again.
          <br><br>
          But, as Dr. Kenneth Korby commented,
          “The LCMS has arrhythmia of the heart.” We
          have tended to focus on the life of the head
